values ((select id from public.sections where slug = $c5299$case$c5299$), (select id from public.lessons where slug = $c5300$case-simple-y-buscada$c5300$), $c5301$case-q03-simple-con-condicion$c5301$, $c5302$error_diagnosis$c5302$, $c5303$intermediate$c5303$, $c5304$Errores de sintaxis y tipos$c5304$, $c5305$Esta consulta falla con `operator does not exist: text = boolean`. ¿Cuál es la causa?$c5305$, $c5306$```sql
SELECT
  id,
  CASE status
    WHEN status = 'delivered' THEN 'Entregado'
    ELSE 'Otro'
  END AS estado
FROM orders;
```$c5306$, $c5307$En la forma simple, PostgreSQL compara `status` con lo que siga a cada `WHEN`. Como `status = 'delivered'` es un booleano, intenta comparar texto con booleano y falla. Correcto: `CASE status WHEN 'delivered' THEN ...` o `CASE WHEN status = 'delivered' THEN ...`.$c5307$, null, null, array[$c5308$case$c5308$,$c5309$sintaxis$c5309$]::text[], 60, true)
