values ((select id from public.sections where slug = $c6652$cte$c6652$), (select id from public.lessons where slug = $c6653$cte-with-pasos$c6653$), $c6654$cte-q04-interpretar-encadenada$c6654$, $c6655$query_interpretation$c6655$, $c6656$intermediate$c6656$, $c6657$CTE encadenadas$c6657$, $c6658$¿Qué devuelve esta consulta sobre TiendaViva?$c6658$, $c6659$```sql
WITH entregas AS (
  SELECT customer_id, total_amount
  FROM orders
  WHERE status = 'delivered'
),
por_cliente AS (
  SELECT customer_id, count(*) AS pedidos, sum(total_amount) AS gasto
  FROM entregas
  GROUP BY customer_id
)
SELECT count(*) AS clientes
FROM por_cliente
WHERE pedidos >= 3;
```$c6659$, $c6660$La primera CTE filtra, la segunda resume por cliente y el `SELECT` final cuenta cuántos clientes cumplen la condición. Cada paso tiene un nombre que explica qué hace.$c6660$, null, null, array[$c6661$cte$c6661$,$c6662$group_by$c6662$,$c6663$aggregate$c6663$]::text[], 70, true)
